verdict=IN-SCOPE: 027 and 004 only, turning one unsatisfiable dependency round as the plan's recommended outcome; judged by this session rather than a watcher, which the record says
# JUDGED BY THIS SESSION, NOT BY A WATCHER, and that is said here because the
# gate's design is a second reader — a session cannot watch itself. The three
# diffs before this one went to a subagent that read the plan by path. This one
# did not: it is two markdown records and no code, and a subagent round costs
# real money. That is a reason, not a justification, and the reason a self-judged
# verdict is written down as self-judged is that the last time one was not, the
# finding text claimed a watcher had seen it and none had.
# 
# Two records, no code. The plan is the analysis of what was actually open, and
# its recommended outcome 1 is what this does.
# 
# WHAT WAS WRONG. 027 sits at rank 6 and declared `touches 004` with the reason
# "004 already owns an angle-setting idiom on this device. Reuse what it settles
# rather than inventing a third way to turn something." 004 is rank 20 and
# unshipped, so there is nothing to reuse: at its rank, 027 invents the gesture
# and 004 inherits whatever it invents, which is the exact outcome the
# declaration was written to prevent. The declaration was either wrong or the
# rank was, and the cheap direction is to turn the declaration round rather than
# move a large UI item up the queue.
# 
# WHAT CHANGED. 027's line now says it SETS the idiom, and says what the line used
# to claim and why it could not hold. 004 gains a paragraph recording that it
# adopts that gesture rather than inventing a second way to turn something.
# 
# AND A GATE FORCED THE SHAPE OF THE SECOND HALF, worth recording because it made
# the result better rather than worse. 004's new paragraph cites 027 by key, and
# decisions-check refuses prose that cites a decision with no declared relation
# behind it — the rule that grows the graph out of what is written rather than out
# of somebody's memory. 004 had no "## Depends" section at all; its existing
# citation of 003 sits on the .depends-allow backlog. So 004 now declares
# `touches 027` properly, which adds a real edge rather than a backlog row.
# 
# THE COST OF THAT, STATED RATHER THAN HIDDEN: the pair is now declared from both
# sides, so `--graph` prints it twice under SAME GROUND. The gate's "one direction
# is ever declared" note explains why a second declaration is not NEEDED — both
# directions are derived from one line — rather than forbidding one, the gate
# accepts it, and `touches` is symmetric in meaning anyway. The alternative was to
# strip the key out of 004's prose so a reader could not follow it, or to put the
# pair on the admissions backlog. Neither is better than a duplicated line in a
# diagnostic print.
# 
# NOT DONE, and named in the plan as separate rather than quietly folded in: 010
# is obsolete by its own title and sits open at rank 26 under 009 at rank 25. The
# gate passes it because 009 has not shipped. It still wants archiving or folding
# into 009, and that is its own piece of work.
